{"step_index":2253,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:58:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:28:38+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:28:39+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/MODEL_CARD.md`\nTotal Lines: 188\nTotal Bytes: 7424\nShowing lines 50 to 188\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n50: \n51: ## 📌 Overview\n52: \n53: **Fluxnat Coder 3B** is a specialized, high-precision cybersecurity and code security intelligence model developed by **Fluxnat**. \n54: Engineered for static analysis and fine-tuned using **Unsloth (QLoRA)** on curated vulnerability datasets, threat intelligence corpora, and structured Chain-of-Thought (CoT) security audit trajectories, **Fluxnat Coder 3B** acts as an autonomous Static Application Security Testing (SAST) analyst and secure code reviewer.\n55: \n56: Unlike generic code models that frequently trigger false safety refusals when auditing real-world security vulnerabilities, **Fluxnat Coder 3B** is completely refusal-free for authorized defensive security analysis, penetration testing verification, and automated vulnerability triage.\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## 🚀 Key Capabilities\n61: \n62: - **🔍 Taint Flow & Root Cause Analysis:** Tracks untrusted input from **Source $\\rightarrow$ Sanitizer $\\rightarrow$ Sink** with explicit causality.\n63: - **🏷️ Deterministic CWE & OWASP Mapping:** Maps discovered flaws directly to MITRE CWE identifiers (CWE-89, CWE-78, CWE-22, CWE-79, CWE-502, CWE-918, etc.) and OWASP Top 10 categories.\n64: - **📊 Objective CVSS Scoring:** Computes vulnerability severity ratings (Critical, High, Medium, Low) and estimated CVSS base metrics.\n65: - **🛡️ Production-Ready Secure Fixes:** Generates drop-in replacements with parameterized queries, safe execution APIs, and canonicalized path operations.\n66: - **⚡ Ultra-Low Latency & Minimal Footprint:** At 3 billion parameters, it fits comfortably into consumer GPUs (4 GB VRAM in 4-bit) and edge environments.\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 🌐 Supported Programming Languages & Stacks\n71: \n72: | Ecosystem | Vulnerabilities Covered |\n73: | :--- | :--- |\n74: | **Python** | SQLi, Command Injection, Path Traversal, Insecure Deserialization (`pickle`/`yaml`), SSRF, Hardcoded Secrets |\n75: | **JavaScript / TypeScript / Node.js** | DOM XSS, `child_process.exec`, Prototype Pollution, Unsafe Regex (ReDoS), JWT misconfigurations |\n76: | **Go** | Unchecked errors, SSRF (`http.Get`), Unsafe Pointer arithmetic, Command execution, Race conditions |\n77: | **C / C++** | Buffer overflows, Use-After-Free, Format string vulnerabilities, Memory leaks, Integer overflows |\n78: | **Java** | JNDI injection, XML External Entity (XXE), SQLi via Hibernate/JDBC, Deserialization |\n79: | **PHP** | File inclusion (`LFI`/`RFI`), SQLi, `eval` injection, Object injection |\n80: | **Infrastructure / DevOps** | Dockerfile root user, exposed ports, unpinned images, `.env` secret leaks |\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 💻 Quickstart Inference\n85: \n86: ### 1. Using Hugging Face `transformers`\n87: \n88: ```python\n89: import torch\n90: from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n91: \n92: MODEL_ID = \"k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\"\n93: \n94: tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID, trust_remote_code=True)\n95: model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n96:     MODEL_ID,\n97:     torch_dtype=torch.float16,\n98:     device_map=\"auto\",\n99:     trust_remote_code=True\n100: )\n101: \n102: messages = [\n103:     {\n104:         \"role\": \"system\",\n105:         \"content\": (\n106:             \"You are Fluxnat Coder 3B, an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding intelligence model created by Fluxnat. \"\n107:             \"Your mission is to perform rigorous source code vulnerability auditing, identify CWE and OWASP Top 10 security flaws, \"\n108:             \"explain attack surfaces and root causes using detailed step-by-step reasoning, and provide production-ready secure remediations.\"\n109:         )\n110:     },\n111:     {\n112:         \"role\": \"user\",\n113:         \"content\": \"\"\"Audit this Node.js endpoint for vulnerabilities:\n114: \n115: app.get('/ping', (req, res) => {\n116:     const host = req.query.host;\n117:     exec(`ping -c 3 ${host}`, (err, stdout) => {\n118:         res.send(stdout);\n119:     });\n120: });\"\"\"\n121:     }\n122: ]\n123: \n124: text = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(messages, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n125: inputs = tokenizer(text, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n126: \n127: outputs = model.generate(\n128:     **inputs,\n129:     max_new_tokens=512,\n130:     temperature=0.2,\n131:     top_p=0.95\n132: )\n133: \n134: response = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0][inputs.input_ids.shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)\n135: print(response)\n136: ```\n137: \n138: ---\n139: \n140: ## 🛠️ Serving with vLLM (Production & API)\n141: \n142: Run an OpenAI-compatible high-throughput inference server:\n143: \n144: ```bash\n145: python -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \\\n146:     --model k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B \\\n147:     --dtype float16 \\\n148:     --max-model-len 4096 \\\n149:     --port 8000\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ---\n153: \n154: ## ⚙️ Training Details\n155: \n156: | Hyperparameter | Value |\n157: | :--- | :--- |\n158: | **Architecture** | 3B Parameter Dense Decoder-Only Transformer |\n159: | **Fine-Tuning Framework** | **Unsloth** + TRL `SFTTrainer` |\n160: | **Method** | QLoRA (4-bit Base Model with 16-bit LoRA Adapters) |\n161: | **LoRA Rank ($r$)** | `64` |\n162: | **LoRA Alpha ($\\alpha$)** | `128` |\n163: | **Target Modules** | `q_proj`, `k_proj`, `v_proj`, `o_proj`, `gate_proj`, `up_proj`, `down_proj` |\n164: | **Learning Rate** | `2e-4` (Cosine Scheduler) |\n165: | **Effective Batch Size** | `16` (Batch size 2 $\\times$ Gradient Accumulation 4 $\\times$ 2) |\n166: | **Sequence Length** | `4,096` tokens |\n167: | **Hardware** | 1x NVIDIA Tesla T4 GPU (Google Colab Free Tier) |\n168: | **Optimizer** | `adamw_8bit` |\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## ⚖️ Responsible Use & Ethical Policy\n173: \n174: **Fluxnat Coder 3B** is designed and released exclusively for:\n175: - ✅ Defensive software security auditing and continuous integration code reviews\n176: - ✅ Assisting development teams in finding and patching security flaws before deployment\n177: - ✅ Educational and academic cybersecurity research\n178: - ❌ Unauthorized penetration testing or attacking systems without explicit written consent is strictly prohibited.\n179: \n180: ---\n181: \n182: <div align=\"center\">\n183: \n184: **Developed with ❤️ by Fluxnat**  \n185: *Next-Generation AI for Cyber Defense*\n186: \n187: </div>\n188: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
